# Nothing of the data is ever committed here. It travels as release assets, which can be deleted
# in one click - which is the whole point of this repository being separate.
#
# Everything is ignored, and the few files this repository really holds are let back in one by one.
# A database or an asset therefore cannot be committed by accident, not even with `git add -A`,
# and not even under a name nobody thought of.
*

!.gitignore
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!.github/
!.github/**

# `git add -f` overrides any ignore file, and nothing written here can stop it; what this file does
# guarantee is that no ordinary `git add`, and no `git add -A`, picks a database up. These patterns
# repeat the obvious shapes so that an exception added above by mistake still does not let one in.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.zst
*.zst.[0-9][0-9][0-9]
*.zip
*.7z
*.tar
*.gz
*.pak
*.lsf
*.lsx
*.loca
manifest.json
